WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.802
Before any certificate moves,

2
00:00:01.802 --> 00:00:06.428
the program establishes what the old
certificate authority actually holds up:

3
00:00:06.428 --> 00:00:09.863
every authority, every template,
every certificate issued,

4
00:00:09.863 --> 00:00:11.825
and every system that trusts them.

5
00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:14.375
Then each template gets
one of four verdicts.

6
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:16.888
Retire it if its consumer is going away.

7
00:00:16.888 --> 00:00:19.900
Migrate it if Intune or
Entra can replace it.

8
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.400
Bridge it if it depends on Active
Directory itself, like domain controllers.

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.312
And retain it only if nothing else can
serve it, with an owner and a review date.

10
00:00:29.312 --> 00:00:34.003
The decision for the PKI administrators:
every template classified,

11
00:00:34.003 --> 00:00:37.212
with a named owner, in the
plan's first four weeks.

12
00:00:37.212 --> 00:00:40.700
And before any of it moves,
what stays has to be safe.
